25rem}.dpv1 .dp-concentration{grid-template-columns:1fr}.dpv1 .dp-why{margin:1.25rem 1rem}.dpv1 .dp-footer{padding:1.1rem 1rem}.dpv1 table{font-size:.85rem}.dpv1 table th,.dpv1 table td{padding:.5rem .55rem}.dpv1 .dp-toptrades{font-size:.78rem}.dpv1 .dp-toptrades th,.dpv1 .dp-toptrades td{padding:.4rem .4rem}.dpv1 .dp-sector-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}\n</style>\n\n  <div class=\"dp-hero\">\n    <div class=\"dp-meta\">\n      <span class=\"dp-date\">2026-05-14</span>\n      <span class=\"dp-sep\">/</span>\n      <span class=\"dp-tag\">BASE (BULL TILT)</span>\n      <span class=\"dp-sep\">/</span>\n      <span class=\"dp-closing-bell\">End-of-session read</span>\n    </div>\n    <h2 class=\"dp-headline\">Mixed tape with a slight risk-on lean.</h2>\n  </div>\n\n  <section class=\"dp-section dp-narr\">\n    <h3>What I noticed today</h3>\n    <p>What stood out next was the sector tape. Health Care (XLV) ran <strong>$69.7M in call premium against $1.2M in puts</strong> &mdash; a net of <span class=\"pos\">$68.5M</span> that led the heatmap. Technology (XLK) was the second-tier read at <span class=\"pos\">$12.1M</span> net, with a 6.5:1 call-to-put ratio. </p>\n    <p>The cracks were in financials and industrials. <strong>XLF inverted</strong> with $4.4M call against $6.2M put for a net of <span class=\"neg\">-$1.8M</span>, and XLI did the same at <span class=\"neg\">-$1.7M</span>. Defense was selective today, not broad &mdash; the tape didn't hedge everything, it hedged the cyclicals.</p>\n    <p>Single-name aggregate flow lined up as <strong>SPY</strong> ($5.2M), <strong>SPX</strong> ($4.3M), <strong>NVDA</strong> ($2.5M) at the top of the notable-flow book. Where the index complex (SPX, SPXW, SPY, QQQ, IWM) shows up in this list is the part I tag and watch the next session &mdash; index-side flow doesn't move like single-name flow.</p>\n    <p>On the dark pool side, NVDA held the top slot at $43.6M with 0 mega-prints. Nothing exotic in the tape, but the mega-print count is the line I watch and it stayed in range.</p>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"dp-section\">\n    <h3>By the numbers</h3>\n    <ul class=\"dp-bullets\">\n      <li>Call premium <strong>$40.11B</strong></li>\n      <li>Put premium <strong>$14.70B</strong></li>\n      <li>Call/Put skew <strong>2.7:1</strong></li>\n      <li>P/C volume <strong>0.60</strong></li>\n      <li>Scenario <strong>BASE (BULL TILT)</strong></li>\n    </ul>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"dp-section\">\n    <h3>Top 10 single-trade events</h3>\n    <p style=\"margin:.2rem 0 .9rem;color:#94a3b8;font-size:.92rem\">Today's largest single-trade notable flow events, ranked by total premium. Observational only &mdash; what stood out, not a to-do.</p>\n    <table class=\"dp-toptrades\">\n      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Ticker</th><th>Strike &middot; Expiry (DTE)</th><th>Type</th><th>Premium</th><th>Vol / OI (V/OI)</th><th>Spot</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr>\n          <td>1</td>\n          <td><strong>SPY</strong></td>\n          <td>$735 \u00b7 2026-05-29 (15d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-neg\">Put</td>\n          <td>$4.1M</td>\n          <td>11,077 / 2,136 (5.2x)</td>\n          <td>$742.43</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>2</td>\n          <td><strong>SPX</strong></td>\n          <td>$7430 \u00b7 2026-07-17 (64d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-pos\">Call</td>\n          <td>$1.9M</td>\n          <td>105 / 261 (0.4x)</td>\n          <td>$7445.11</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>3</td>\n          <td><strong>SPX</strong></td>\n          <td>$7650 \u00b7 2026-07-17 (64d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-pos\">Call</td>\n          <td>$958.8K</td>\n          <td>187 / 1,567 (0.1x)</td>\n          <td>$7444.64</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>4</td>\n          <td><strong>SPX</strong></td>\n          <td>$7690 \u00b7 2026-07-17 (64d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-pos\">Call</td>\n          <td>$813.7K</td>\n          <td>86 / 46 (1.9x)</td>\n          <td>$7444.8</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>5</td>\n          <td><strong>NVDA</strong></td>\n          <td>$235 \u00b7 2026-06-18 (35d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-pos\">Call</td>\n          <td>$603.1K</td>\n          <td>9,972 / 26,955 (0.4x)</td>\n          <td>$225.57</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>6</td>\n          <td><strong>SLV</strong></td>\n          <td>$69 \u00b7 2026-06-30 (47d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-pos\">Call</td>\n          <td>$601.0K</td>\n          <td>474 / 1,700 (0.3x)</td>\n          <td>$79.325</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>7</td>\n          <td><strong>STX</strong></td>\n          <td>$900 \u00b7 2026-08-21 (99d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-pos\">Call</td>\n          <td>$537.9K</td>\n          <td>129 / 4 (32.2x)</td>\n          <td>$818.72</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>8</td>\n          <td><strong>AMD</strong></td>\n          <td>$445 \u00b7 2026-05-15 (1d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-pos\">Call</td>\n          <td>$466.2K</td>\n          <td>7,570 / 3,085 (2.5x)</td>\n          <td>$445.14</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>9</td>\n          <td><strong>QQQ</strong></td>\n          <td>$705 \u00b7 2026-06-18 (35d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-neg\">Put</td>\n          <td>$462.6K</td>\n          <td>2,292 / 5,228 (0.4x)</td>\n          <td>$714.42</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>10</td>\n          <td><strong>NVDA</strong></td>\n          <td>$225 \u00b7 2026-05-15 (1d)</td>\n          <td class=\"val-pos\">Call</td>\n          <td>$425.1K</td>\n          <td>141,649 / 114,630 (1.2x)</td>\n          <td>$225.88</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n    <p class=\"dp-tide\">Today's largest single-trade event was a SPY $735 put dated 2026-05-29 at $4.1M in premium.</p>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"dp-section\">\n    <h3>Sector heatmap</h3>\n    <table class=\"dp